- How do you handle edge cases where aggregated data exceeds quality thresholds?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to quantify cross-cutting costs for a telemetry pipeline under real-world constraints (mobile energy, network variability, privacy).

## Key Concepts
- Cost-benefit modeling for streaming telemetry
- Adaptive sampling and batching trade-offs
- On-device resources vs backend costs
- Privacy, regulatory, and consent considerations
- Rollout strategy and break-even analysis

## Code Example
```javascript
function computeCBA(params){
  const {events, batchSize, rate, energyPerEvent, dataCost} = params;
  const batches = Math.ceil(events / batchSize);
  const energy = batches * energyPerEvent * (rate/100);
  const data = events * dataCost * (rate/100);
  return {energy, data, batches};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would opt-in rate and drift affect the CBA over time?
- How would you validate and adjust thresholds in production?

## Why This Is Asked
